Z||000000||JetroGT||09-15-1999||12:36 AM||||Last weekend I took a trip down to Oakbrook IL for Fierorama. I wated at a Mcdonalds in Kenosha for the Fiero Fanitics. There was about 6 Fieros that showed up. Then we all took off on the high way down to Oakbrook. The show was great! Quite a few custom mods and kits. 1 Aldino, 2 305's, 1 Mera, about 10 different V8 swaps which included a North Star, and two corvette engines. They also had a lot of 3800 type swaps. Some with the super chargers on them. My clunker didn't win any thing. I was parked next to Rodney Dickmans parts tent. Bob Steiger was also there. I finaly found a tan GT steering wheel which I bought from Bob for a hundred bucks. The show got cut short because it started raining. I'll try to get some of the pictures of the Aldino posted. It's AWSOME!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||09-15-1999||02:19 AM||||the Aldino rocks!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/aldino.jpg"> ||||reg||14
